{
  "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
  "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nPAUL D. CLEMENT, ESQ. Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nZACHARY D. TRIPP, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, in support of the Petitioner.\nKANNON K. SHANMUGAM, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "WesternGeco LLC",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress enacted Section 271(f) to address this Court's decision in Deepsouth and to prohibit a specific domestic act of infringement with foreseeable foreign consequences. Congress targeted a specific domestic act, the supply of components from the United States, with a particular intent, that the components be combined abroad in a way that, if it happened in the United States, would constitute infringement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But all of the activity occurs -- not only does the activity occur abroad sweeping the high seas, but the one who is causing the injury is not the infringer; it's the customer of the infringer. Do we have another situation like that where -- where you can collect from the infringer on the basis of activity by the customer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "ION Geophysical Corporation",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What the foreign combiners of the components do on the high seas is not infringement of a U.S. patent at all, which is why I think the presumption against extraterritoriality is really a misfit here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And you have to resort to the general principle, which is, in U.S. law, if somebody's injured domestically by domestic conduct, there's no rule that says that, in order to calculate the compensatory damages to make them whole, if you have to include in your calculation some foreign thing, there's no rule against that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I'm looking for that principle."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Tripp",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I think there's two pieces to that. I think one is that (f) is, I think, narrower than you're describing in your hypothetical."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: The D.C. Circuit did that with Empagran follow-up in -- in a case which you may not have read. Tell me if you haven't read it; I'll stop."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Professor Yelderman",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the -- the other place that I think is helpful to look at this is Professor Yelderman's amicus brief, which does a nice job of walking through the doctrine both of causation-in-fact and proximate cause in the federal circuit when dealing with problems that are analogous to these."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Tripp",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We're asking the rule -- affirmatively to adopt this rule as a matter of Section 284, the general damages provision that applies all throughout the Patent Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So it's not something special about this damages provision; you're saying as to any damages provision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, what is the -\u00ad what is the domestic injury?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I -- I had one question the Chief Justice agreed I could ask. Suppose the Petitioner had a foreign subsidiary in the Bahamas and it used that in order to conduct a sweeping operation, so it sells -- it sells the device to the -- to the subsidiary, and the subsidiary then uses it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shanmugam",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHANMUGAM: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The presumption against extraterritoriality applies with particular force to the Patent Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shanmugam",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHANMUGAM: Justice Sotomayor, Petitioner, in fact, did get a reasonable royalty, to the tune of $22 million, which compensates for the act of infringement; that is to say, the initial factual injury from supplying the infringing component from the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0014",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But -- but it seems to me that you're confining the right of the Petitioner to decide how it's going to use its own patent. Isn't it up to the Patent Owner to decide how it's going to capitalize on its patent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0015",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, if Congress had prohibited the foreign combination, wouldn't that be the end of the case? Would you still argue that you'd have to analyze whether the damages provision applies extraterritorially?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0016",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, there -- there are differences between this case and RJR Nabisco, which I won't go into, but if -- if you have a liability provision that says there is liability for acts that are committed abroad, what sense does it make to say, well, although Congress thinks there should be liability for these acts committed abroad, we have to analyze the -- the remedial provisions separately to see whether they wanted any remedy for these acts that are committed abroad."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0017",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Why does that make any sense whatsoever?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0001-0018",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What are they?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus brief",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0002-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now that's not just hypothetical because an amicus brief cites to us the Marvel case where that really happened."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner, like the government, thinks that the same rule should apply to Section 271(f) as to Section 271(a)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Isn't that exactly how the copyright law is applied under the"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0002-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the risk of runaway jury awards here certainly does present substantial comity concerns."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84523d702c6971305b3c621eccb6e8ad4a7aa8b36525ea548dc89d0d06291f09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84523d702c69-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It was, in fact, brought in the Southern District of Texas, where both of these companies are located."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1011",
      "confidence": 0.0,
